From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(instance): pin parse_field duplicate-detection bits for
 contract allow/deny

### What
Pins the `seen` bitmap bits used by `parse_field` for `[contract] allow` (bit 19) and `deny` (bit 20): repeating either key must fail with `DuplicateField`, while a single occurrence parses cleanly.

### Why it matters
`builder.mark(1 << N)` is the only duplicate guard. Shifting right (`1 >> 19 == 0`) marks bit 0, already seen from `schema_version`, so every config carrying `allow`/`deny` would be rejected as a duplicate of the wrong field. The existing duplicate test only pins `instance.id` (bit 1).

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| `mark(1 << 19)` -> `mark(1 >> 19)` (contract.allow) | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `mark(1 << 20)` -> `mark(1 >> 20)` (contract.deny) | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-instance --lib parse_field_duplicate_detection`.

Spec-Ref: ginux instance-config parser (seen-bitmap duplicate-field contract)

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
index cfb78bd5..0b7b4ec9 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
@@ -3251,4 +3251,20 @@ failure = "stop"
             .unwrap();
         assert_eq!(c.contract_deny.as_slice().len(), 1);
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn parse_field_duplicate_detection_pins_contract_allow_deny_bits() {
+        let dup_allow = VALID.replace("allow = []", "allow = []\nallow = [\"syscall.clock_*\"]");
+        assert_eq!(
+            InstanceConfig::parse(dup_allow.as_bytes()),
+            Err(ConfigError::DuplicateField)
+        );
+        let dup_deny = VALID.replace("deny = []", "deny = []\ndeny = [\"syscall.mount*\"]");
+        assert_eq!(
+            InstanceConfig::parse(dup_deny.as_bytes()),
+            Err(ConfigError::DuplicateField)
+        );
+        // single occurrence still parses cleanly
+        assert!(InstanceConfig::parse(VALID.as_bytes()).is_ok());
+    }
 }
